            <ArticleTitle>Pain management discussion forum: serious interaction among frequently used drugs for chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>170-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15360288.2014.911798</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A query and response regarding a patient who was taking high-dose tramadol and duloxetine is presented. The patient developed serotonin syndrome. Risks for this clinically important drug interaction and management of the syndrome are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
